{
  "duration": 64.22,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.119,
      "end": 0.28,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.779,
      "end": 1.679,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.159,
      "end": 3.24,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.799,
      "end": 7.519,
      "text": "Now in this problem, a train runs at seventy-two kilometer per hour"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.0,
      "end": 8.739,
      "text": "without halts,"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.099,
      "end": 12.5,
      "text": "but its average speed with halts drops to sixty kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.099,
      "end": 14.019,
      "text": "The question is"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.559,
      "end": 16.719,
      "text": "asking us to find the stoppage time per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.279,
      "end": 18.119,
      "text": "Think of it this way,"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.559,
      "end": 20.079,
      "text": "in one hour without any halts,"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.379,
      "end": 22.359,
      "text": "the train would cover seventy-two kilometer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.92,
      "end": 23.219,
      "text": "but"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.539,
      "end": 24.459,
      "text": "because of halts,"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.819,
      "end": 27.42,
      "text": "it covers only sixty kilometer in one hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.92,
      "end": 28.579,
      "text": "The difference,"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.039,
      "end": 30.359,
      "text": "seventy-two minus sixty,"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.76,
      "end": 31.959,
      "text": "which is twelve kilometer,"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.5,
      "end": 36.02,
      "text": "is the distance the train could have covered if it had not stopped."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.34,
      "end": 39.899,
      "text": "Now let us find how much time it takes to cover those twelve kilometer"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.319,
      "end": 43.399,
      "text": "at the running speed of seventy-two kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.759,
      "end": 49.139,
      "text": "We know time is equal to distance divided by speed, so time is equal to twelve divided by seventy-two hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.68,
      "end": 51.819,
      "text": "After simplifying, we get one by six hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.18,
      "end": 53.739,
      "text": "Now convert this into minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.259,
      "end": 58.719,
      "text": "One by six hours is equal to sixty divided by six, which is ten minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.079,
      "end": 61.139,
      "text": "So the train stops for ten minutes every hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.539,
      "end": 64.22,
      "text": "Hence, the correct answer is option C."
    }
  ],
